From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:47:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: keep the camera firmware up 5 s
 after a stream

An application that stops a stream and starts the next, as video calls
and photo apps do, waits for a firmware start each time. macOS keeps the
T8140's firmware up 5 s after a stream. A hold on the J604 measured the
warm start with it and the ISP powering down after the 5 s. Keep the
firmware 5 s by default; fw_keep_ms=0 stops it at once.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
index 673f8dad07..fe6273d9a1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/isp/isp-cam.c
@@ -2193,12 +2193,13 @@ static int isp_configure_capture(struct apple_isp *isp)
  * (T8132: 239 ms of a 516 ms open, most of it installing the sensor).
  * With fw_keep_ms, a stream that ends leaves it running and idle for that
  * long, and an open within that time uses it as is. Its power domains
- * stay on meanwhile. 0 (the default) stops it at once, as before.
+ * stay on meanwhile. The default keeps it 5 s, as macOS keeps the T8140's;
+ * 0 stops it at once.
  */
-static unsigned int fw_keep_ms;
+static unsigned int fw_keep_ms = 5000;
 module_param(fw_keep_ms, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(fw_keep_ms,
-		 "Keep the camera firmware running this many ms after a stream (default: 0, stop at once)");
+		 "Keep the camera firmware running this many ms after a stream (default: 5000)");
 
 /* Stop firmware left running after a stream; takes video_lock. */
 void apple_isp_fw_cool(struct apple_isp *isp)
-- 
